            <div xml:id="d828">

                <pb facs="0971" n="853" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg853"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.111 Zizianoff, Nina Princess</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic">July 22,
                        1927</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 1.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7686</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s cabled
                    Instruction No. 198, June 30, 3 P.M., I have the honor to report that, after
                    consultation with Mr. Bigelow’s lawyer, the Embassy addressed a note to the
                    Foreign Office on July 5th, in the sense outlined by the Department, regarding
                    the suit brought by Princess Zizianoff against Mr. Donald F. Bigelow.</p>
                <p>I am now in receipt of a reply, dated July 20th, in which the Foreign Office
                    states that, while divergencies of views have appeared in the notes exchanged
                    between this Embassy and the Ministry for Foreign Affairs concerning the scope
                    of the expression “personal immunity”, it has been recognized on both sides that
                    the meaning of “immunity <pb facs="0972" n="854" xml:id="pg854"/> from the
                    jurisdiction of the courts” had never been given to this formula. The Foreign
                    Office adds that the statements made to the press by Mr. Bigelow are personal
                    acts and cannot under any heading be considered as official acts.</p>
                <p>A copy and translation of the aforementioned note are to-day being transmitted to
                    Mr. Bigelow’s lawyer for his information.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sheldon
                    Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d828-a1.xml" xpointer="d828-a1"/>
            </div>
